    {
      "id": "p3-b03-pass-01",
      "kind": "conversation",
      "title": "Catering order",
      "body": null,
      "transcript": "N: Questions 32 through 34 refer to the following conversation.\nW: Good morning, Lakeside Catering. How can I help you?\nM: Hi, I'd like to order lunch for a training session next Tuesday. There will be forty people.\nW: Certainly. We have a sandwich platter for twelve dollars per person, or a hot buffet for eighteen.\nM: The buffet sounds nice, but our budget is limited. Could we do the sandwiches with a salad added?\nW: Of course. The salad is three dollars extra per person. We can deliver by eleven-thirty.\nM: Perfect. Please put the order under Brightwell Solutions.",
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "p3-b03-pass-02",
      "kind": "conversation",
      "title": "Printer repair",
      "body": null,
      "transcript": "N: Questions 35 through 37 refer to the following conversation.\nM: Hi Rosa, the printer on the third floor is jammed again. Can you take a look?\nW: I'm in a meeting until noon. Have you tried the reset button?\nM: Twice. It still says the paper tray is empty, but I just filled it.\nW: That sounds like a sensor problem. I'll call the repair company this afternoon and ask them to send a technician tomorrow.\nM: Thanks. In the meantime, I'll use the printer on the second floor.\nW: Good idea. I'll put a sign on this one so nobody wastes time with it.",
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "p3-b03-pass-03",
      "kind": "conversation",
      "title": "Interview scheduling",
      "body": null,
      "transcript": "N: Questions 38 through 40 refer to the following conversation.\nW: Hello, Mr. Patel. This is Anna from Harmon Industries. We received your application for the project engineer position.\nM: Thank you for calling. I'm very interested in the job.\nW: We'd like to invite you for an interview. Would next Wednesday at two o'clock work?\nM: Unfortunately, I have a flight that morning, but I'll be back by noon. Could we make it three instead?\nW: Three is fine. Please bring your portfolio and two references. The office is on the fourth floor.\nM: Understood. Should I ask for you at reception?\nW: Yes, and I'll meet you in the lobby.",
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "p3-b03-pass-04",
      "kind": "conversation",
      "title": "Hotel room problem",
      "body": null,
      "transcript": "N: Questions 41 through 43 refer to the following conversation.\nM: Excuse me, I'm in Room 512. The heating isn't working, and it's quite cold.\nW: I'm very sorry, sir. Let me check whether we have another room available.\nM: I'd appreciate that. I have a meeting early tomorrow and need some rest.\nW: I can offer you Room 608 on the sixth floor. It's a larger room at no extra cost.\nM: That's perfect. Could someone help me with my luggage?\nW: Certainly. A porter will be there in five minutes, and I'll send up some tea as well.",
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "p3-b03-pass-05",
      "kind": "conversation",
      "title": "Planning a client dinner",
      "body": null,
      "transcript": "N: Questions 44 through 46 refer to the following conversation.\nW: Kevin, have you booked the restaurant for the client dinner on the fifteenth?\nM: I called Marlowe's yesterday. They can seat us at seven, but the private room is already taken.\nW: That's too bad. We wanted a quiet space to discuss the contract.\nM: They suggested a table near the back garden. It's usually calm after eight.\nW: Then let's move the reservation to eight-fifteen. Is there a vegetarian option? One of the clients doesn't eat meat.\nM: Yes, they have several. I'll confirm the new time and send the menu to everyone.",
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "p3-b03-pass-06",
      "kind": "conversation",
      "title": "Software training",
      "body": "TRAINING TIMETABLE — Accounting software\nMonday 10 A.M.    Invoices\nWednesday 2 P.M.    Reports\nThursday 9 A.M.    Reports\nFriday 11 A.M.    Payroll",
      "transcript": "N: Questions 47 through 49 refer to the following conversation.\nM: Welcome, everyone. Before we begin the training on the new accounting software, does anyone have questions about the schedule?\nW: I have a client meeting on Wednesday afternoon. Is there another session I could attend?\nM: Let me look at the timetable. The session on reports is offered twice, so you could join the one on Thursday morning.\nW: That works. And is the session on invoices recorded in case I miss something?\nM: Yes, all sessions are recorded and posted on the intranet the next day.",
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "p3-b03-pass-07",
      "kind": "conversation",
      "title": "Car rental",
      "body": null,
      "transcript": "N: Questions 50 through 52 refer to the following conversation.\nW: Good afternoon. I reserved a compact car for three days under the name Harper.\nM: One moment, Ms. Harper. I see your booking. We're out of compact cars at the moment, but I can offer you a midsize car at the same price.\nW: That's fine, as long as it has a navigation system.\nM: All our midsize cars do. Would you like to add insurance? It's fifteen dollars a day.\nW: My credit card already covers rentals, so I'll skip that.\nM: Then please sign here, and I'll bring the car around to the entrance.",
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "p3-b03-pass-08",
      "kind": "conversation",
      "title": "Return of a purchase",
      "body": null,
      "transcript": "N: Questions 53 through 55 refer to the following conversation.\nM: Hello, I bought this desk lamp last week, but the switch stopped working. I'd like to return it.\nW: I'm sorry about that. Do you have the receipt?\nM: Yes, here it is. I'd prefer a replacement rather than a refund.\nW: Unfortunately, that model is sold out. We expect a new shipment on the twentieth. I can hold one for you, or give you store credit now.\nM: I'll take the store credit. I also need some light bulbs.\nW: No problem. I'll apply the credit to your purchase today.",
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "p3-b03-pass-09",
      "kind": "conversation",
      "title": "Budget approval",
      "body": null,
      "transcript": "N: Questions 56 through 58 refer to the following conversation.\nW: Dennis, did the finance committee look at our request for new laptops?\nM: They did. They approved half of it, which means we can buy ten laptops this quarter.\nW: That's good news. We can start with the sales team since their computers are the oldest.\nM: I agree. The committee wants a short report on how the laptops are used after three months.\nW: Fine. I'll ask the vendor for a discount since we're ordering in bulk.\nM: Good idea. Let me know what they say by Friday.",
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "p3-b03-pass-10",
      "kind": "conversation",
      "title": "Office relocation",
      "body": "NEW BUILDING — DEPARTMENT LOCATIONS\n5th floor: Marketing, Design\n4th floor: Legal\n3rd floor: Finance\n2nd floor: Human Resources\n1st floor: Reception, Cafeteria",
      "transcript": "N: Questions 59 through 61 refer to the following conversation.\nM: Hi Leila, I've received the list of department locations for the new building. Have you seen it?\nW: Not yet. Where will Marketing be?\nM: Let me check the chart. Marketing will be on the fifth floor, next to Design. Human Resources moves to the second floor.\nW: Good. I was afraid we'd be in the basement. When can we start moving boxes?\nM: The movers come on Saturday, so you can pack on Friday afternoon.\nW: Okay. I'll let my team know.",
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "p3-b03-pass-11",
      "kind": "conversation",
      "title": "Customer survey results",
      "body": null,
      "transcript": "N: Questions 62 through 64 refer to the following conversation.\nW: I've finished analyzing the customer survey. Overall satisfaction rose to eighty-four percent.\nM: That's up from seventy-eight last year. What improved the most?\nW: Delivery speed. The new tracking feature got very positive comments.\nM: And the weak points?\nW: Mostly the website's search function. Several customers said it was hard to find products.\nM: Then let's ask the web team to improve it before the holiday season. Can you prepare a summary for tomorrow's meeting?\nW: Sure, I'll include a few charts.",
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "p3-b03-pass-12",
      "kind": "conversation",
      "title": "Travel reimbursement",
      "body": null,
      "transcript": "N: Questions 65 through 67 refer to the following conversation.\nM: Ms. Cho, I'm submitting my travel expenses from the conference in Chicago. Is the form the same as last year?\nW: Almost. This year you need to upload receipts online instead of attaching paper copies.\nM: Got it. Does the company reimburse taxi rides?\nW: Yes, but only if the ride is under fifty dollars. For anything over that, we'd like you to use the train.\nM: Most of my rides were around thirty. I did take one for sixty-five, though, because of a late flight.\nW: Add a short note explaining that, and I'll approve it as an exception.",
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "p3-b03-pass-13",
      "kind": "conversation",
      "title": "New employee orientation",
      "body": null,
      "transcript": "N: Questions 68 through 70 refer to the following conversation.\nW: Welcome to Corbin Logistics, Mr. Reyes. I'm Tanya from Human Resources. Let me show you around.\nM: Thank you. Should I sign any documents today?\nW: Yes, the tax forms and the confidentiality agreement. Then we'll set up your computer and email.\nM: Great. When do I meet my team?\nW: At eleven, you'll have a short meeting with your supervisor, Ms. Huang. After lunch, the safety training begins.\nM: Will I need a parking permit?\nW: Yes, I'll give you a temporary one. The permanent badge arrives next week.",
      "image": null
    }
  ],
